From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Naeem Malik <malik2015naeem@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:19:08 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: power-cycle the J313 panel the boot loader handed
 over

On a MacBook Air (M1, 2020, J313) with DCP 13.5 the boot loader leaves
the panel on.  The first dcp_poweron() then finds it enabled
(set_device_enabled 1 -> 1) and only sets a mode: the firmware does not
power up its video interface, assert HPD or load its LTM block, and logs
that it could not find the Backlight service.  Brightness swaps are
taken and the published level follows them, but the panel stays at the
boot level.  A DPMS off/on runs the firmware's full power-on sequence,
and every brightness change after it reaches the panel.

Give the J313 panel that cycle once, on DCP 13.5, when the boot loader
handed it over lit: an available simple-framebuffer whose "panel" points
at it.  The first power-on then cancels the swap watchdog, disconnects
the AV service and powers the pipe off, as dcp_poweroff() does for an
internal panel, before powering on.  The node outlives the handover, so
the cycle is marked done when it runs, and a later bind does not repeat
it; a bind that fails before the first power-on leaves it for the retry.
Other panels and firmware are unchanged.

Measured on a MacBook Air (M1, 2020, J313, DCP firmware 13.5) running
linux-aurora 7.2.11: brightness changes reach the panel straight after
boot, after s2idle suspend/resume, and after a boot with the lid closed,
where the boot loader still hands the panel over and the cycle completes
without timeouts.  Before, backlight writes had no visible effect until
one DPMS cycle.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Naeem Malik <malik2015naeem@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 36bef1a058f514d56ee073262d0b91e8cf16c10f)
[j604: k610 drm sync: dcp.c conflict; the panel is matched by its first compatible only, and the J516C EDID make/product read (dropped with the J516C EDID wiring) is not carried.]
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-internal.h |  3 ++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c          | 81 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 73 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-internal.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-internal.h
index 5b9f50b60d..76315fa9e7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-internal.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-internal.h
@@ -632,6 +632,9 @@ struct apple_dcp {
 	/* clear all surfaces on init */
 	bool surfaces_cleared;
 
+	/* J313: the first dcp_poweron() cycles the panel handed over lit */
+	bool panel_cold_poweron;
+
 	/* enable CRC calculation */
 	bool crc_enabled;
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index 0ccb2d0f7d..6cff32e770 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -4143,6 +4143,13 @@ int dcp_typec_prepare_route(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 	return ready ? 0 : -ETIMEDOUT;
 }
 
+/*
+ * Set once the boot loader's panel has been power-cycled.  The framebuffer
+ * node outlives the handover, so a later bind must not take it again; a bind
+ * that fails before the cycle leaves it for the retry.
+ */
+static bool dcp_panel_handover_taken;
+
 void dcp_poweron(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct apple_dcp *dcp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
@@ -4260,6 +4267,25 @@ void dcp_poweron(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			dcp_dptx_connect(dcp, 0);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * J313 on DCP 13.5 finds its panel already on from the boot loader
+	 * (set_device_enabled 1 -> 1), so the first power-on only sets a mode:
+	 * the firmware never powers up its video interface or LTM block and
+	 * logs that it could not find the Backlight service.  It then takes
+	 * the levels Linux swaps in and reports them back, but the panel stays
+	 * at the boot level until a DPMS cycle.  Give it that cycle once, as
+	 * dcp_poweroff() runs it for an internal panel.
+	 */
+	if (dcp->panel_cold_poweron) {
+		dcp->panel_cold_poweron = false;
+		dcp_panel_handover_taken = true;
+		dev_info(dcp->dev, "power-cycling the panel handed over by the boot loader\n");
+		cancel_delayed_work(&dcp->swap_watchdog_wq);
+		if (dcp->avep)
+			av_service_disconnect(dcp);
+		_dcp_poweroff(dcp);
+	}
+
 	switch (dcp->fw_compat) {
 	case DCP_FIRMWARE_V_12_3:
 		iomfb_poweron_v12_3(dcp);
@@ -5179,6 +5205,34 @@ static bool dcp_panel_is_j313(const char *compatible)
 	return compatible && !strcmp(compatible, "apple,panel-j313");
 }
 
+/*
+ * The boot loader hands a panel over lit as an available simple-framebuffer
+ * whose "panel" points at it, until the first power-on has cycled it (see
+ * dcp_panel_handover_taken).
+ */
+static bool dcp_panel_handed_over(struct device_node *panel_np)
+{
+	struct device_node *fb, *panel;
+	bool lit = false;
+
+	if (dcp_panel_handover_taken)
+		return false;
+
+	for_each_compatible_node(fb, NULL, "simple-framebuffer") {
+		if (!of_device_is_available(fb))
+			continue;
+		panel = of_parse_phandle(fb, "panel", 0);
+		lit = panel == panel_np;
+		of_node_put(panel);
+		if (lit) {
+			of_node_put(fb);
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return lit;
+}
+
 static int dcp_comp_bind_pipe(struct device *dev, struct device *main, void *data)
 {
 	struct device_node *panel_np;
@@ -5301,17 +5355,22 @@ static int dcp_comp_bind_pipe(struct device *dev, struct device *main, void *dat
 		if (of_property_read_string_index(panel_np, "compatible", 0,
 						  &compatible))
 			compatible = NULL;
-		/*
-		 * Only this panel.  The backlight device's maximum is this
-		 * value, so 100% asks the firmware for DCP_J313_MAX_NITS.
-		 */
-		if (dcp_panel_is_j313(compatible) &&
-		    dcp->brightness.maximum > DCP_J313_MAX_NITS) {
-			dcp->brightness.maximum = DCP_J313_MAX_NITS;
-			if (dcp->brightness.nits > (int)DCP_J313_MAX_NITS)
-				dcp->brightness.nits = DCP_J313_MAX_NITS;
-			dev_info(dev, "capping panel backlight at %u nits\n",
-				 DCP_J313_MAX_NITS);
+		if (dcp_panel_is_j313(compatible)) {
+			dcp->panel_cold_poweron =
+				dcp->fw_compat == DCP_FIRMWARE_V_13_5 &&
+				dcp_panel_handed_over(panel_np);
+			/*
+			 * Only this panel.  The backlight device's maximum is
+			 * this value, so 100% asks the firmware for
+			 * DCP_J313_MAX_NITS.
+			 */
+			if (dcp->brightness.maximum > DCP_J313_MAX_NITS) {
+				dcp->brightness.maximum = DCP_J313_MAX_NITS;
+				if (dcp->brightness.nits > (int)DCP_J313_MAX_NITS)
+					dcp->brightness.nits = DCP_J313_MAX_NITS;
+				dev_info(dev, "capping panel backlight at %u nits\n",
+					 DCP_J313_MAX_NITS);
+			}
 		}
 
 		of_node_put(panel_np);
